From: omarchy-dragon-sl7 <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:01:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: Disable the empty pcie3 card reader slot

SL7 local: arm64: dts: qcom: x1e80100-romulus13: Disable the empty pcie3 card reader slot

The shared romulus DTSI enables pcie3 and pcie3_phy for the RTS5261 card
reader of the 15 inch Surface Laptop 7. The 13.8 inch has no card reader
(Windows lists only two PCIe root ports there: Wi-Fi and NVMe), so on
romulus13 the controller never trains a link.

pcie-qcom votes the maximum OPP at probe and lowers it only after link-up,
so the empty controller keeps a 15.75 GB/s peak interconnect vote on
DDR (the largest on the system), the Gen4 x8 PHY with its pipe, aux and
rchng clocks, and the tcsr_pcie_8l_clkref_en XO reference on for as long as
the machine is awake.

Disable both nodes in romulus13 only. romulus15 is untouched. Nothing else
needs a change:
  - pcie3_port0 (reset and wake GPIOs) is a child of the disabled
    controller and is not probed.
  - The pcie3_default pinctrl state is referenced only by pcie3, so it is
    simply never applied; the three pads stay in their reset state.
  - The PHY supplies vreg_l3c and vreg_l3e are shared with other
    consumers and stay as they are. There is no dedicated pcie3 slot
    regulator in the romulus DT (vreg_nvme belongs to pcie6a).
  - The gcc node lists pcie3_phy as a clock parent. hamoa.dtsi leaves the
    PHY disabled by default, so boards without pcie3 already run this way.

Rationale: RUNTIME-PLAN.md section 4.1 (C1). Expected on the 13.8 inch: the
llcc_mc peak falls from 15753000 to 7876500 kBps and the PCIe3 PHY, clocks
and GDSC go off. Not measured yet.

Origin: ours
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (candidate: romulus13 card reader fix)
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus13.dts
@@ -156,6 +156,21 @@
 };
 
 /*
+ * No card reader on the 13.8 inch: the RTS5261 behind pcie3 is a 15 inch
+ * (romulus15) part and the slot is empty here, so the link never trains.
+ * Leaving the controller enabled keeps the maximum OPP and the 15.75 GB/s
+ * peak interconnect vote that pcie-qcom casts at probe, plus the 8 lane PHY
+ * and its clocks, for as long as the machine is awake.
+ */
+&pcie3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&pcie3_phy {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/*
  * Touch digitizer (GTCH, MSHW0460 on units with a Surface Touch G6 module):
  * HID over SPI in QSPI mode on QUP1 SE2. Wiring from the ACPI GTCH device:
  * SpiSerialBusV2 40 MHz mode 0, IRQ GPIO51, reset GPIO48, VDD enable GPIO64.
